A||||10||Ronen||All fieros have sunroof cut outs?||||5||
Z||000000||Ronen||05-13-2001||03:39 PM||||Is it true that ALL Fieros were manufactured with a sunroof cut outs? And, to make a a non sunroof Fiero all I have to do is replace the fiberglass top with a sunroofed fiberglass unit?||||reg||5
Z||000001||TheFiero64||05-13-2001||03:48 PM||||Yep, It is true. It only took me an afternoon to add the sunroof of my parts car to my 88, You just remove the roof section as one piece with the a pillars and put the sunroof one on.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spektyr||05-13-2001||03:48 PM||||I was out in a junkyard looking at Fiero's for the first time last week (only had my Fiero for a few weeks now).<P>I was in one and happened to notice that it didn't have the headliner, and did not have a sunroof.  It did indeed have a frame in the exact shape of my sunroof in the roof of the car, but exactly what would be involved in the swap I don't know.  Would probably be pretty easy to cut the roof out using the frame as a guide and simply transplant the donor sunroof in.  (If you're careful, you wouldn't have to repaint this way.)<P>Of course you might want to wait for the more knowledgable to post on this...<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||05-13-2001||04:19 PM||||You can't just cut the hole out in a non-sunroof skin.  The sunroof skin has  sections molded into it for mounting the sunroof, the sunroof gasket and the trim piece to transition from the sunroof to the headliner.  If you just cut a hole in a non-sunroof skin you would have no way to mount these items, you'd just have a hole!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 05-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spektyr||05-13-2001||06:20 PM||||Ah... good thing no one listens to my advice, eh?<P>hehe<P>Then again... maybe with superglue?  Okay, maybe not.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||05-13-2001||10:37 PM||||My Fiero doesn't have a sunroof cutout <P>------------------<BR>Jeff (AOL IM - FieroTT)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">     <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||12
Z||000006||DJRice||05-13-2001||10:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>My Fiero doesn't have a sunroof cutout <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Mine does, and its black.  Wanna Trade?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadaver||05-14-2001||12:54 AM||||Yes it does. They all do. The cutout is not in the roof panel its in the spaceframe under the fiberglass panel. All the years and all the models and all the options there is only one spaceframe.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Will||05-14-2001||12:21 PM||||The '88's have a different frame from other years. They front suspension mounting points changed as did the location of the rear strut towers.||||reg||1
Z||000009||cadaver||05-14-2001||01:38 PM||||yes you are right the 88"s are different in that aspect.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Rodrv6||05-14-2001||04:14 PM||||But even all the 88's had a sunroof cutout in the space frame.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
